# Chat Command Implementation Summary
## What Was Created
A new `chat` command for OpenClaw that provides a simple, terminal-based interface for interacting with the AI agent.
## Files Created/Modified
### New Files
1. **`openclaw-standalone/src/cli/chat-cli.ts`** - Main chat command implementation
2. **`openclaw-standalone/CHAT_COMMAND.md`** - Quick reference guide
3. **`openclaw-standalone/CHAT_USAGE.md`** - Complete usage documentation
4. **`openclaw-standalone/test-chat.sh`** - Test script for the chat command
### Modified Files
1. **`openclaw-standalone/src/cli/program/command-registry.ts`** - Registered the chat command
2. **`openclaw-standalone/README.md`** - Added chat command to documentation
## Features Implemented
✅ **Simple Terminal Interface** - Clean readline-based chat UI
✅ **Gateway Integration** - Uses existing GatewayChatClient for WebSocket communication
✅ **Real-time Streaming** - Displays AI responses as they're generated
✅ **Session Management** - Supports custom session keys for context isolation
✅ **Model Override** - Can specify different models per chat session
✅ **Configuration Integration** - Reads from existing OpenClaw config
✅ **Error Handling** - Clear error messages and connection status
✅ **Graceful Exit** - Multiple exit methods (exit, quit, Ctrl+C)
✅ **Provider Support** - Works with all configured providers (Google Antigravity, etc.)
✅ **Channel Delivery** - Optional flag to send responses to messaging channels
## Usage
```bash
# Basic usage
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat
# With options
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat --session work --model google-antigravity/claude-opus-4-5-thinking
# Remote gateway
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat --url ws://remote:18789 --token TOKEN
# Enable channel delivery
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat --deliver
```
## Command Options
t:5(Option,Description,Default)[`--url <url>`,Gateway WebSocket URL,`ws://127.0.0.1:18789` `--token <token>`,Gateway auth token,From config `--session <key>`,Session identifier,`main` `--model <model>`,AI model to use,From config `--deliver`,Send to channels,`false`]
## Architecture
```
Chat CLI (chat-cli.ts)
    ↓
GatewayChatClient (tui/gateway-chat.ts)
    ↓
GatewayClient (gateway/client.js)
    ↓
WebSocket Connection
    ↓
Gateway Server (running on ws://127.0.0.1:18789)
    ↓
AI Agent (with configured model/provider)
```
## How It Works
1. **Initialization**
   - Loads OpenClaw configuration
   - Resolves gateway URL, token, agent ID, and session key
   - Creates GatewayChatClient instance
2. **Connection**
   - Connects to gateway via WebSocket
   - Waits for "connected" event
   - Displays connection status
3. **Message Loop**
   - Uses Node.js readline for input
   - Sends user messages via `client.sendChat()`
   - Listens for `agent.chunk` events for streaming responses
   - Handles `agent.done` and `agent.error` events
4. **Exit**
   - User types "exit" or "quit"
   - Or presses Ctrl+C
   - Stops client and closes readline interface
## Key Implementation Details
### Event Handling
```typescript
client.onEvent = (evt) => {
  if (evt.event === "agent.chunk") {
    // Stream text chunks to stdout
    process.stdout.write(payload.text);
  } else if (evt.event === "agent.done") {
    // Response complete, show prompt
    rl.prompt();
  } else if (evt.event === "agent.error") {
    // Display error and recover
    console.error(error);
  }
};
```
### Message Sending
```typescript
await client.sendChat({
  sessionKey,
  message: input,
  deliver: opts.deliver,
  thinking: undefined,
  timeoutMs: undefined,
});
```
### Configuration Resolution
- Uses existing `loadConfig()` from OpenClaw
- Resolves agent ID with `resolveDefaultAgentId()`
- Normalizes session key with `normalizeMainKey()`
- Falls back to sensible defaults
