## Troubleshooting
### Gateway not running
```bash
# Start gateway
bun scripts/run-node.mjs gateway
```
### Connection refused
```bash
# Check gateway port
cat ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json | grep -A 3 '"gateway"'
# Verify gateway is listening
netstat -an | grep 18789
```
### No response from agent
```bash
# Check gateway logs
tail -f /tmp/openclaw/openclaw-*.log
# Verify model configuration
cat ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json | grep -A 5 '"agents"'
```
## Conclusion
The chat command provides a simple, effective way to interact with OpenClaw's AI agent directly from the terminal. It's perfect for quick conversations, testing, and debugging without needing to set up messaging channels.
The implementation is minimal (~200 lines), uses existing OpenClaw infrastructure, and provides a clean user experience.